.Dd October 22, 2026
.Dt AMARCHY 1
.Os UP-Term
.Sh NAME
.Nm Amarchy ,
.Nm amarchy-menu ,
.Nm amarchy-gui
.Nd Super-key shortcuts for the whole Amiga
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm Amarchy
.Op Cm CX_PRIORITY Ar n
.Nm amarchy-menu
.Cm menu Ar node
.Nm amarchy-menu
.Cm viewer
.Nm amarchy-gui
.Cm menu Ar node
.Nm amarchy-gui
.Cm viewer
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a commodity, listed in Exchange as AMARCHY, that binds the Left Amiga key
(called Super) plus a letter, digit or function key to an action: a menu
command or slash command of an UP-Term window, a new tab, a program to
start.
Install starts it at every boot from a block in S:User-Startup.
Only the keys of the key file are taken; every other Left Amiga key goes to
the program as before.
Left Amiga + M, Left Amiga + N, Left Amiga + the
mouse and any row with Ctrl are never bound, so the reset keys stay safe.
While an UP-Term window is active it matches the keys itself and
.Nm
leaves them alone.
.Pp
.Nm amarchy-menu
is the program the keys start:
Left Amiga + Space runs
.Ql amarchy-menu menu root ,
a short list filtered by typing,
and Left Amiga + K runs
.Ql amarchy-menu viewer ,
the list of every key.
.Nm amarchy-gui
is the drawn version of the same two screens: its own borderless window with
an icon in front of each row.
The setting
.Ql menu-style = graphical ,
.Ql menu-style = text
or
.Ql menu-style = minimal
in
.Pa ENVARC:up-term/up-term
(before the first section; default graphical) chooses which program Left Amiga
+ Space and Left Amiga + K start; Left Amiga + Alt + Space and Left Amiga + Alt
+ K start the other one.
.Ql minimal
starts
.Nm amarchy-gui
as plain text rows: no border, no icons, two colours (the fg and bg settings,
else the screen's own pens), a group row ends in
.Ql \ > .
The setting
.Ql amarchy-app-icons = generic ,
.Ql amiga
or
.Ql none
chooses the icons of app rows.
The icons come from a table made when the kit is built (dist/menu-icons in
the source), so a row of
.Pa keymap.user
cannot name an icon.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ENVARC:up-term/keymap
The shipped key file (a copy is in ENV:up-term/keymap, read first).
Every Install replaces it; a different old file is first saved as keymap.bak.
.It Pa ENVARC:up-term/keymap.user
Your own rows.
A row replaces the row for the same key;
.Ql super+t = none
unbinds one.
.It Pa UP-Term:Amarchy/Themes/NAME.theme
The shipped GUI themes of the drawn menu (the Omarchy colour themes; the default is tokyo-night).
.It Pa ENVARC:Amarchy/themes/NAME.theme
Your own GUI themes; a file of the same name as a shipped one wins.
To add one, copy an Omarchy
.Pa colors.toml
(keys accent, background, foreground, dark_foreground, optional mode = "light") to this drawer under the new name,
then pick it under Style > Theme in the menu or in the Menu theme row of UP-Term Prefs (Amarchy page).
It applies the next time the menu opens.
An unknown or unreadable theme name draws the compiled-in tokyo-night.
The terminal's own colours (Terminal theme, super+shift+t) are separate.
.El
.Pp
Each row reads
.Dl super[+shift][+alt][+rshift]+KEY = action ; label | category
Actions are menu:id, viewer, tab:new, tab:close, tab:next, tab:prev,
tab:goto N, menuid:NAME, slash:/command, run:command, open:uterm,
rexx:script and win:verb [argument]. The verbs are cycle, front, back, zip,
fullwidth, fullscreen, save, restore, move, size, focus, closedrawers, screen
and title.
Lines starting with a semicolon are comments.
.Sh ARexx
The port AMARCHY takes STATUS (hits, rows, enabled and active), RELOAD (read
the key files again), RUN
.Ar n
(do row n of the table), SHOW (the key viewer) and QUIT.
.Dl rx \(dqaddress AMARCHY RELOAD\(dq
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr UPTerm 1
